							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">If you haven&#039;t joined Amiestreet.com yet, get on it - two good reasons<br /><br />1. It&#039;s Indie Hip Hop Week<br />It&#039;s the first day of Amie Street&#039;s hip hop shopping spree. Thousands of songs are being released (starting free of course), including albums from artists J Dilla, Andre Nickatina, Dru Down, Mac Dre, Public Enemy and Too &#036;hort , to name just a few. They won&#039;t be free for long… click here to view all the new hip hop releases.<br /><br />2. Eclipse® Sets the Stage™ Final Round <b>(Blue Scholars are in the final round)</b><br />Congratulations to the five finalists in the Eclipse Sets the Stage Competition. The final Round of voting has begun! Vote for your favorite and you could win a pair of tickets to the show, and the winning band gets a trip to New York for a CMJ showcase, a stay at a famous hotel, and &#036;10,000! Sweet.<br />And don&#039;t forget this week&#039;s featured artists! We have the daughter of music royalty, avant-garde jazz and sweet <br /><br /><a href="http&#58;//www.amiestreet.com" target="_blank">www.amiestreet.com</a><br /><br />The Five Finalists<br />&nbsp;These United States <br />&nbsp;The Epochs <br />&nbsp;Casey Shea <br />&nbsp;Eli &quot;Paperboy&quot; Reed <br />&nbsp;Blue Scholars <br /><br /></td>
