							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php#1">MASS LINE FORUMS</a> / <a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?board=2.0">The Dialogue</a> / <a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3091.msg35331#msg35331">Re: More Seattle Times on Hip Hop</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: August 10, 2007, 09:30:43 am
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">It is truly amazing how ignorant some people are about hip hop and it&#039;s positive effects on our city.&nbsp; I&#039;ve been around the music scene her for a minute, and it&#039;s amazing the amount of community work and positive influence the local hip hop community has and does. I haven&#039;t scene anything like it since the activism of the punk scene in the late 80&#039;s / early 90&#039;s here. Still not much press happening about that aspect of it though.&nbsp; I know it&#039;s sexier to write about violence, but it would be great to see an article about all the good hip hop does for our world. Seems the press thinks writing about local groups and their business is the balance, but that&#039;s only a small aspect of the community. It was great to hear Piece and Blak talk about this on KUOW yesterday. Maybe the Time and PI will cover this more in depth soon.</td>
						</tr>
